\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Freedom of expression \u8212  and, in less lofty terms, the freedom to make juicy fiction \u8212  has long warred with the regime\u8217 s exhortation to \u8220 tell China\u8217 s story well,\u8221  something Xi Jinping has urged on both artists and diplomats. As the writer Han Dong shrugs in a poem, describing flowers squinted at through smog: \u8220 Even if I see them I don\u8217 t remember them / Even if I remember them I can\u8217 t write about them.\u8221 }
